Q: Page Factory @FindBy A: <p>You can try to use <a href="https://github.com/hhrzc/papaya-injection" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/hhrzc/papaya-injection</a></p>
<p>This library allows to set xpath/css to annotation parameter or separatelly in the defined file</p>
<p>File key-value way:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@Telemetry(&quot;pages/home-page.telemetry&quot;)
public interface HomePage {
    @Sensor(&quot;products&quot;)
    WebElementSupplier productsMenu();
}
</code></pre>
<pre><code>home-page.telemetry:
</code></pre>
<p><code>products=//div[@class='shop-menu pull-right']//li/a[@href='/products']</code></p>
<p>Annotation way (Start with <code>$</code>):</p>
<pre><code>@Telemetry(&quot;pages/home-page.telemetry&quot;)
public interface HomePage {
    @Sensor(&quot;$//div[@class='shop-menu pull-right']//li/a[@href='/products']&quot;)
    WebElementSupplier productsMenu();
}
</code></pre>

Q: Getting Biome to format SVG A: <p>As the biome [html formatting support](<a href="https://biomejs.dev/reference/configuration/#htmlformatterenabled" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://biomejs.dev/reference/configuration/#htmlformatterenabled</a>) is still experimental  the html formatter ( <code>html.formatter.enabled</code>)  has to be turned on in the configuration file as well</p>
<pre><code>  &quot;html&quot;: { 
    &quot;experimentalFullSupportEnabled&quot;: true,
    &quot;formatter&quot;: { &quot;enabled&quot;: true } 
  },
</code></pre>
